* Pregnant or breastfeeding women;
* History of periodontal treatment within the previous 6 months;
* Continuous use of oral antiseptics, systemic antibiotics, corticosteroids, nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drugs, immunosuppressive agents, estrogen, selective estrogen receptor modulators, or medications that may affect bone metabolism (such as alendronate, calcitonin, and others) within the previous 6 months;
* Presence of systemic conditions that may alter the host response to periodontal treatment (such as diabetes, human papillomavirus infection, or Down syndrome) or that require antibiotic prophylaxis before dental treatment (such as mitral valve prolapse);
